Normalise spill paths to forward slashes

The Windows job caught this, and only the Windows job could have: the relative
path in the stub notice came from Path::display(), so on Windows the model read
"spill\20260923\..." while every test and the docs say "spill/...". The separator
is now normalised at the source — that string is written for the model to read,
and a path whose shape changes per platform is a path nobody can trust. Joining
it back still works on Windows, which accepts both separators.

Also gave the breaker test more slack: a 150ms cooldown with a 220ms wait is
fine on a laptop and optimistic on a loaded CI runner.
